    },
    "preceding_nonempty_paragraphs": [
      {
        "container_path": "models/XBeach/raw/source_code/trunk/doc/manual/XBeach_manual_master.docx",
        "member": "word/document.xml",
        "start_xml_ordinal": 26267,
        "body_paragraph_zero_based": 691,
        "direct_body_paragraph_zero_based": 623,
        "paragraph_id": "6644A37A",
        "text": "In the groundwater model there are three mechanisms for the vertical exchange of groundwater and surface water: 1) submarine exchange, 2) infiltration and 3) exfiltration. The rate of exchange between the groundwater and surface water (S) is given in terms of surface water volume, and is defined positive when water is exchanged from the surface water to the groundwater."
      },
      {
        "container_path": "models/XBeach/raw/source_code/trunk/doc/manual/XBeach_manual_master.docx",
        "member": "word/document.xml",
        "start_xml_ordinal": 26288,
        "body_paragraph_zero_based": 693,
        "direct_body_paragraph_zero_based": 625,
        "paragraph_id": "2A83C1BD",
        "text": "Infiltration and exfiltration can only occur in locations where the groundwater and surface water are not connected. Infiltration takes place when surface water covers an area in which the groundwater level is lower than the bed level. The flux of surface water into the bed is related to the pressure gradient across the wetting front."
      }
    ],
    "following_nonempty_paragraphs": [
      {
        "container_path": "models/XBeach/raw/source_code/trunk/doc/manual/XBeach_manual_master.docx",
        "member": "word/document.xml",
        "start_xml_ordinal": 26405,
        "body_paragraph_zero_based": 696,
        "direct_body_paragraph_zero_based": 628,
        "paragraph_id": "30A95BFF",
        "text": "In (2.70) the surface water-groundwater exchange flow of infiltration (Sinf) is calculated using the effective hydraulic conductivity (K), the surface water pressure at the bed () and the thickness of the wetting front ()."
      },
      {
        "container_path": "models/XBeach/raw/source_code/trunk/doc/manual/XBeach_manual_master.docx",
        "member": "word/document.xml",
        "start_xml_ordinal": 26518,
        "body_paragraph_zero_based": 698,
        "direct_body_paragraph_zero_based": 630,
        "paragraph_id": "3244C7BA",
        "text": "Since the groundwater model is depth-averaged and cannot track multiple layers of groundwater infiltrating into the bed, the wetting front thickness is reset to zero when there is no available surface water, the groundwater exceeds the surface of the bed, or the groundwater and the surface water become connected. In addition, all infiltrating surface water is instantaneously added to the groundwater volume, independent of the distance from the bed to the groundwater table. Since the groundwater model neglects the time lag between infiltration at the beach surface and connection with the groundwater table a phase error may occur in the groundwater response to swash dynamics"
      }
    ],
    "table_cell": null,
    "text_method": "Saved display-field substitution plus w:t; equation objects are not transcribed."
  },
